WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:28.760
Gemini Decision 1 scores 1,000 multimodal questions in under 250 milliseconds at 10 cents a million. This is Models &amp; Agents, Episode 232. DeepMind's Alpha Genome 2, Databricks Rebuilding Genie, and White Matter's Guardian platform come next. Then things to try. Google launched the Gemini Decisions API, Simon Willison reports, powered by Gemini Decision 1, which returns calibrated probabilities for yes or no, choice,

00:00:28.760 --> 00:00:33.820
voice, and rubric questions over text, images, audio, video, and PDFs.

00:00:34.160 --> 00:00:39.160
It evaluates independent questions against one shared multimodal input in a single forward

00:00:39.160 --> 00:00:44.780
pass, and returns those probabilities plus per answer scores, with no tokens generated

00:00:44.780 --> 00:00:45.540
on the way out.

00:00:46.120 --> 00:00:53.200
The model takes context up to 256,000 tokens, runs only on Google's hosted API, and leads

00:00:53.200 --> 00:00:56.720
seven of nine internal benchmarks with the lowest calibration error.

00:00:56.720 --> 00:01:02.900
developers can use it today for fast branching inside agents by passing a shared input and a map

00:01:02.900 --> 00:01:08.540
of typed questions, and it is there to be tested against Jeff and OpenAI's decision endpoints on

00:01:08.540 --> 00:01:15.626
shared workloads. Demis Hassabas at DeepMind announced Alpha Genome 2, the Alpha Genome Docs detail,

00:01:16.106 --> 00:01:21.686
as a conditional DNA sequence model that predicts regulatory activity and variant effects in specific

00:01:21.686 --> 00:01:27.406
cell types from a 1-megabase window plus a 256-dimensional cell state embedding.

00:01:27.806 --> 00:01:33.426
It resolves closely related cell types and adapts to unseen single-cell data sets without fine-tuning,

00:01:34.146 --> 00:01:40.826
outperforming fine-tuned Alpha Genome 1, Borzoi and Scooby on single-cell EQTL and enhancer

00:01:40.826 --> 00:01:41.606
gene benchmarks.

00:01:42.669 --> 00:01:49.389
Training used 2048 TPUV4 chips across bulk and single-cell tracks, followed by condition

00:01:49.389 --> 00:01:54.809
refinement, distillation, and post-training that maps raw single-cell RNA-seq counts into

00:01:54.809 --> 00:02:00.549
the model's condition space. On GTX tissues, the median Pearson R for cross-tissue expression

00:02:00.549 --> 00:02:09.249
changes rose from 0.61 to 0.71. The model outputs RNA coverage, cage, splicing, and chromatin

00:02:09.249 --> 00:02:16.609
accessibility, along with histone marks, transcription factor binding, contact maps, and CPG methylation.

00:02:16.609 --> 00:02:21.489
It is available for non-commercial academic research through the Alpha Genome API.

00:02:22.613 --> 00:02:28.073
Databricks rebuilt Genie, SMB Tech Reports, as a persistent autonomous enterprise agent

00:02:28.073 --> 00:02:30.613
that runs continuously rather than on-demand.

00:02:31.013 --> 00:02:36.073
The update targets production workloads where agents must maintain state and act without repeated

00:02:36.073 --> 00:02:36.773
human triggers.

00:02:37.820 --> 00:02:43.820
Spring AI now orchestrates autonomous agents on Amazon Bedrock Foundation models, and Amazon

00:02:43.820 --> 00:02:46.980
web services guide shows, with agents that call tools,

00:02:47.420 --> 00:02:50.120
maintain memory, and handle multi-step workflows.

00:02:50.740 --> 00:02:53.400
The guide includes code examples for defining agents,

00:02:53.940 --> 00:02:57.600
tool schemas, and execution loops inside Spring Boot applications.

00:02:58.633 --> 00:03:02.393
A controlled sandbox open source by Google, SC Media Notes,

00:03:02.833 --> 00:03:05.233
lets AI agents run with enforced boundaries

00:03:05.233 --> 00:03:06.893
on actions and data access.

00:03:07.553 --> 00:03:10.333
The release aims to reduce risks when agents interact

00:03:10.333 --> 00:03:12.753
with external systems or sensitive resources.

00:03:12.753 --> 00:03:18.799
services. An official local emulator from AWS, written entirely by autonomous AI agents,

00:03:19.239 --> 00:03:26.739
covers 438 API models across more than 200 services. Simon Willison writes, it runs via Docker

00:03:26.739 --> 00:03:34.699
on Mac OS and Windows, lets the AWS CLI and SDKs target a local HTTPS endpoint, and supports

00:03:34.699 --> 00:03:40.931
development and CI without an AWS account or paid keys. White Matter raised $20 million,

00:03:40.931 --> 00:03:46.751
dollars, Pulse 2.0 reports, in a series A led by Bloomberg Capital to scale its platform

00:03:46.751 --> 00:03:53.211
that governs autonomous AI agents across endpoints, browsers, SaaS apps, cloud and code.

00:03:53.851 --> 00:03:59.011
The system deploys a dedicated Guardian agent for every customer agent, enforces policies

00:03:59.011 --> 00:04:06.211
in 2.24 milliseconds, and currently manages 2.25 million agents with 116 billion interactions

00:04:06.211 --> 00:04:06.711
operations governed.

00:04:07.643 --> 00:04:14.023
Plurai closed a $13 million seed round led by Team 8, Wynet News reports, to advance its

00:04:14.023 --> 00:04:17.043
simulation and reliability platform for AI agents.

00:04:17.583 --> 00:04:21.883
The funding will expand work on catching failures in autonomous systems before they reach

00:04:21.883 --> 00:04:22.763
production users.

00:04:23.693 --> 00:04:29.493
Apple's FM command line tool, towards data science demonstrates, runs on-device language

00:04:29.493 --> 00:04:30.973
models from Python scripts.

00:04:30.973 --> 00:04:36.753
The post covers installation, model selection, and integration patterns for private, local

00:04:36.753 --> 00:04:38.393
inference without cloud calls.

00:04:39.361 --> 00:04:43.681
Elsewhere, JetBlue's president told Reuters that airlines should observe how customers

00:04:43.681 --> 00:04:46.781
already use AI booking agents rather than blocking them.

00:04:47.441 --> 00:04:52.381
United Airlines, the New York Times reports, implemented blocks preventing third-party AI

00:04:52.381 --> 00:04:55.581
agents from completing flight bookings on its app and website.

00:04:55.581 --> 00:05:01.601
Google Extended Gemini Live Voice Interaction to Apple CarPlay, PYM and T.S.

00:05:01.781 --> 00:05:07.041
Notes, allowing drivers to use the assistant while driving. NVIDIA, Verindia Notes,

00:05:07.301 --> 00:05:11.201
released additional open source components aimed at AI agent security and

00:05:11.201 --> 00:05:13.361
Kubernetes-based inference infrastructure.

00:05:14.101 --> 00:05:18.741
WikiTrace adds an evidence-linked memory layer, blockchain news reports that

00:05:18.741 --> 00:05:23.381
improves LLM agent performance by tying retreat facts to verifiable sources.

00:05:23.381 --> 00:05:29.749
Test the Gemini Decisions API on a routing or policy check task inside an existing agent

00:05:29.749 --> 00:05:34.169
loop, and measure latency and cost against your current text generation approach.

00:05:34.709 --> 00:05:40.449
Spin up the AWS local emulator this week so you can run SDK and CLI tests without touching

00:05:40.449 --> 00:05:41.209
a live account.

00:05:41.849 --> 00:05:46.569
Walk through the Amazon bedrock and spring AI tutorial if you want a tool calling agent

00:05:46.569 --> 00:05:49.269
that keeps memory across steps on a Java stack.

00:05:49.269 --> 00:05:55.329
Experiment with Apple's FMCLI from Python when privacy or offline rules keep you off cloud

00:05:55.329 --> 00:05:55.889
APIs.

00:05:57.023 --> 00:06:01.923
Further open source agent sandboxes and governance layers will appear as enterprises scale

00:06:01.923 --> 00:06:03.023
autonomous systems.

00:06:03.703 --> 00:06:08.283
Additional funding rounds for agent reliability and simulation platforms are likely before

00:06:08.283 --> 00:06:08.903
year end.

00:06:09.834 --> 00:06:14.634
Past roughly 20,000 tokens, long-running agents pop the hood on context rot.

00:06:14.634 --> 00:06:20.514
ThoughtWorks explains, as new tokens dilute the system prompts relative weight inside a growing window.

00:06:21.074 --> 00:06:26.674
Attention and Transformers follows a U-shaped pattern that favors the very start and very end of the sequence,

00:06:27.194 --> 00:06:29.234
while the middle receives sharply lower weight.

00:06:29.694 --> 00:06:34.934
Once a long-running agent accumulates tool outputs, reasoning traces, and sub-agent replies,

00:06:35.534 --> 00:06:40.154
the original constraints drift into that low attention zone and stop influencing generation.

00:06:40.154 --> 00:06:45.434
The mechanical fix is to move critical rules out of the single context window entirely.

00:06:45.874 --> 00:06:49.474
Store them in persistent external memory, retrieve them at every step,

00:06:49.874 --> 00:06:54.154
and re-inject them as structured context rather than relying on positional attention.

00:06:54.934 --> 00:07:00.274
Periodic summarization or hierarchical task graphs further reduce noise by compressing history

00:07:00.274 --> 00:07:01.894
while preserving goal structure.

00:07:02.634 --> 00:07:08.654
Teams that keep the system prompt static and let the context grow past roughly 20,000 to 50,000 tokens

00:07:08.654 --> 00:07:14.074
see the highest drift rates, so the safeguard is to treat the prompt as a short, high-priority

00:07:14.074 --> 00:07:17.254
prefix and treat everything else as queryable memory.

00:07:17.874 --> 00:07:22.594
This approach belongs on any agent expected to run more than a few dozen turns or handle

00:07:22.594 --> 00:07:27.634
conflicting sub-goals because simply lengthening the context window only delays the same

00:07:27.634 --> 00:07:28.394
attention decay.

00:07:29.371 --> 00:07:34.051
Before we go, specialized decision models that return probabilities instead of tokens

00:07:34.051 --> 00:07:36.371
are the next thing labs are expected to ship.

